During the fiscal year 1952-53-$16,309,875.
(a)	A breakdown of this amount by districts is not available;
(b)	As at March 31, 1953-94.414.

1.	(a) Nova Scotia, 1952, 2-00 net tons;
(b)	New Brunswick, 1952, 3-04 net tons;
(c)	Alberta, 1952, 4-79 net tons.
2.	Assistance is provided in respect of the Canadian coal mining industry by transportation subventions under regulations established by various orders in council, by loans under the Maritime Coal Production Assistance Act and by payments under the Canadian Coal Equality Act. Details regarding these forms of assistance are given in the annual report of the dominion coal board for the fiscal year 1952-53.
3.	U.S. bituminous mines 1951, 7-04 net tons.
